NALA Interactive Funnel Architecture

Psychology-Driven Funnel Structure for Mell

⸻

CORE OBJECTIVE

This is NOT a “questionnaire.”

This is:

A Guided Psychological Transformation Journey.

The user should feel:
✔ emotionally engaged
✔ curious
✔ understood
✔ excited
✔ progressively committed

The goal is NOT:

“Sell a course.”

The goal is:

“Make the user feel they are beginning a new future.”

⸻

TARGET FEELING THROUGHOUT THE FUNNEL

The funnel should feel:
✔ modern
✔ premium
✔ AI-assisted
✔ personalized
✔ smooth
✔ fast-moving
✔ visually rewarding

The user should NEVER feel:
❌ exhausted
❌ interrogated
❌ overwhelmed
❌ “stuck in a long form”

⸻

IDEAL STRUCTURE

Total Sections:

7–9 sections

Total Interactions:

~14–18 interactions max

⚠️ IMPORTANT:
Short interactions.
Fast momentum.
Minimal typing.

⸻

IMPORTANT UX RULES

Every 2–3 interactions:

Add:
✔ progress bar movement
✔ small animation
✔ encouraging text
✔ transition effects

Examples:
✔ “Great choice.”
✔ “Building your personalized roadmap…”
✔ “Analyzing your profile…”
✔ “Calculating your career path…”
✔ “Almost done…”

⸻

SECTION 1 — QUICK ENTRY

“Let’s get to know you”

⸻

Screen 1 — DATE OF BIRTH

Question:

What is your date of birth?

⚠️ IMPORTANT:
DO NOT use age ranges.

Use:

iPhone-style Date Picker Wheel

Like:

* BetterMe
* Apple onboarding
* premium mobile apps

⸻

Psychology:

✔ feels premium
✔ creates micro-commitment
✔ creates interaction momentum
✔ increases personalization feeling

⸻

⚠️ HARD STOP CONDITION:
If user is under 18:
Show:

Currently, NALA programs are available for applicants ages 18+ only.

END FLOW.

⸻

Screen 2 — CRIMINAL BACKGROUND FILTER

Question:

Do you currently have a criminal background that may prevent professional licensing?

Options:
✔ No
✔ Yes

⚠️ If YES:
Stop flow.

Message:

Unfortunately, we are currently unable to continue the qualification process.

⸻

Psychology:

✔ professionalism
✔ trust
✔ legitimacy
✔ qualification seriousness

⸻

SECTION 2 — CURRENT LIFE STATUS

“Where are you today?”

Goal:
Create awareness of the gap between current life and desired future.

⸻

Screen 3 — EMPLOYMENT STATUS

Question:

What is your current work situation?

Options with visuals:
✔ Employee
✔ Self-employed
✔ Between jobs
✔ Student
✔ Other

⸻

Recommended Visuals:

* tired office worker
* contractor
* delivery driver
* warehouse worker
* student

⸻

Screen 4 — CURRENT MONTHLY INCOME

Question:

What is your current monthly income?

Options:
✔ Under $2,000
✔ $2,000–$4,000
✔ $4,000–$6,000
✔ $6,000+

⸻

Screen 5 — FINANCIAL SATISFACTION

Question:

How satisfied are you with your current financial situation?

Use:

Slider (1–10)

⸻

Psychology:

✔ activates dissatisfaction
✔ creates emotional gap
✔ increases openness to change

⸻

SECTION 3 — FUTURE DESIRES

“Where do you want to be?”

Goal:
Future visualization.

⸻

Screen 6 — FUTURE INCOME GOAL

Question:

What monthly income goal would you like to reach within the next 4–6 months?

Options:
✔ $4k+
✔ $6k+
✔ $8k+
✔ $10k+

⚠️ IMPORTANT:
Do NOT promise income.
This is user aspiration only.

⸻

Screen 7 — EMOTIONAL VISUALIZATION

Question:

If you had an extra $6,000 every month, how would you most likely use it?

Options WITH HIGH-QUALITY EMOTIONAL IMAGES:
✔ Family vacation in the Caribbean
✔ Luxury vehicle
✔ Bigger home
✔ More time with family
✔ Paying off debt
✔ Building investments/business

⸻

CRITICAL:

This section should feel:

emotional and aspirational.

NOT:
“money flex.”

⸻

Psychology:

✔ future identity projection
✔ emotional dopamine
✔ visualization effect

⸻

SECTION 4 — CONNECTION TO THE PROFESSION

“Why locksmithing?”

Goal:
Create emotional alignment with the profession.

⸻

Screen 8 — PREVIOUS LOCKSMITH EXPERIENCE

Question:

Have you ever used a locksmith service before?

Options:
✔ Yes
✔ No

⸻

Screen 9 — WHAT ATTRACTS YOU MOST?

Question:

What interests you most about becoming a locksmith?

Options WITH VISUALS:

✔ Independence & flexible schedule
Image:
locksmith with service van

✔ High income potential
Image:
professional locksmith working

✔ Starting my own business
Image:
business owner

✔ Working with my hands
Image:
technical hands-on work

✔ A profession AI cannot easily replace
Image:
AI vs real-world trade

✔ Safe & vault work
Image:
luxury safe opening

✔ Helping people in stressful situations
Image:
family locked outside home being helped

⸻

Psychology:

✔ identity alignment
✔ purpose
✔ emotional connection
✔ anti-AI positioning

⸻

SECTION 5 — LIFESTYLE FIT

“Is this a fit for your life?”

Goal:
Make user feel:

“This fits ME personally.”

⸻

Screen 10 — AVAILABLE TIME

Question:

How much time can you realistically dedicate each week to learning?

Options:
✔ 2–4 hours
✔ 5–8 hours
✔ 8+ hours

⸻

Screen 11 — WORK STYLE

Question:

What type of work lifestyle fits you best?

Options WITH IMAGES:
✔ Office routine
✔ Field work & movement
✔ Independent work
✔ Flexible schedule

⸻

Psychology:

✔ self-matching effect
✔ personalization illusion

⸻

SECTION 6 — INTERNAL COMMITMENT

“Readiness”

Goal:
Create psychological commitment.

⸻

Screen 12 — SERIOUSNESS LEVEL

Question:

How serious are you about changing your career this year?

Use:

Slider (1–10)

⸻

Screen 13 — MAIN OBJECTION

Question:

What is currently holding you back the most?

Options:
✔ Money
✔ Fear of starting
✔ Lack of time
✔ Lack of knowledge
✔ Not knowing where to begin

⸻

Psychology:

✔ surfaces objections
✔ emotional honesty
✔ future CRM personalization

⸻

SECTION 7 — AI ANALYSIS EXPERIENCE

“Building your personalized roadmap…”

⚠️ THIS SECTION IS EXTREMELY IMPORTANT.

Goal:
Create:

AI personalization illusion

⸻

Use:

✔ animated loading screens
✔ moving progress bars
✔ AI-style transitions

⸻

Suggested sequence:

✔ “Analyzing your goals…”
✔ “Matching your profile…”
✔ “Calculating your ideal path…”
✔ “Building your personalized roadmap…”
✔ “Preparing your next-step recommendation…”

⸻

Recommended duration:

8–15 seconds max.

⚠️ DO NOT OVERDO THIS.

Needs to feel:
✔ believable
✔ smooth
✔ premium

NOT:
❌ fake
❌ cheesy

⸻

SECTION 8 — PERSONALIZED RESULT

“Your Recommended Path”

Goal:
Emotional peak moment.

⸻

Show:

✔ roadmap
✔ milestones
✔ estimated progression timeline
✔ certification stages
✔ skill development path

⸻

IMPORTANT:

Position carefully.

Use:
✔ career language
✔ certification language
✔ opportunity language

DO NOT use:
❌ “get rich”
❌ “guaranteed income”
❌ “financial freedom”

⸻

SECTION 9 — PRICE REVEAL + LOW FRICTION ENTRY

⚠️ IMPORTANT:
This is NOT where the funnel “sells.”

The funnel already sold emotionally earlier.

This section simply:

lowers friction.

⸻

Headline:

Start Today For Just $299

⸻

Financing Structure:

Then:

$50/month for 24 months

⸻

Small Transparent Text:

Total Program Price: $1,499

Flexible financing available for qualified applicants.

⸻

CTA Suggestions:

✔ Start My Journey
✔ Build My Future
✔ Continue My Enrollment
✔ Unlock My Roadmap

⸻

CRITICAL PSYCHOLOGY NOTE

The user should feel:
NOT:

“I’m buying a course.”

BUT:

“I’m starting a new chapter in my life.”

⸻

COMPLIANCE NOTES

VERY IMPORTANT FOR META / GOOGLE:

Avoid:
❌ “Make money fast”
❌ “Guaranteed income”
❌ “Financial freedom fast”
❌ unrealistic earnings claims

Prefer:
✔ Career
✔ Skills
✔ Certification
✔ Profession
✔ Flexible work
✔ Business opportunity
✔ Skilled trade

⸻

FINAL NOTE FOR MELL

This funnel is NOT:

a form.

It is:

a behavioral conversion system.

The sequencing of emotions matters MORE than the questions themselves.

Correct emotional progression:

1. Curiosity
2. Personal relevance
3. Pain awareness
4. Future visualization
5. Identity alignment
6. Emotional investment
7. AI personalization
8. Low-friction commitment

If executed correctly, this can become one of the most valuable conversion assets inside the entire NALA eco
